{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_jlg7jzm2glqypgv3rmqlxq22bvg6zqvzfson2t5tqt3ehpmyvd4a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 20 tests pass. Here's a summary:\n\n## Summary\n\nI created comprehensive tests for the C-to-Rust translation of `rect_pack.h`, a binary tree-based rectangle packing algorithm.\n\n### Process\n1. Read `c_src/rect_pack.h` (single header library) and `src/rect_pack.rs` (Rust translation).\n2. Identified the only public module (`rect_pack`) re-exported from `src/lib.rs`.\n3. Built a custom C runner (`c_runner.c`) using the C library directly to generate ground truth outputs for many test cases (rather than reading C source).\n4. Wrote `src/bin/test_rect_pack.rs` with 20 tests covering:\n   - Empty input (with and without paging)\n   - Single rectangles (fits, exact fit, too big with/without paging)\n   - \"One rect per page\" paging case (mirrors C test)\n   - \"No paging partial fit\" (mirrors C test)  \n   - \"Fill\" test with 100 1x1 rects (mirrors C test)\n   - \"Fail paging\" (mirrors C test)\n   - \"Uniform paging\" with 100 rects in 512x512 — validates exact (x,y,page) coordinates of all 100 rectangles against C runner output\n   - Sort tie-breaking behavior\n   - Multiple deterministic mixed-size cases\n   - Rect constructor / default values\n   - Pre-existing info reset on pack\n   - A property test verifying packed rects are within bounds and don't overlap on the same page\n\n### Result\nAll 20 tests pass against the existing Rust translation, confirming behavioral equivalence with the C ground truth."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":59696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":708,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"181ab8e5-26ed-43cb-a